    {
      "id": "troilus-and-cressida/sceneV_35.10/p@215978",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "AENEAS.\nMy lord, you do discomfort all the host.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "troilus-and-cressida/sceneV_35.10/p@215978/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 7,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "troilus-and-cressida/sceneV_35.10/p@215978/line-2",
          "start": 8,
          "end": 48,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 6317933,
        "end": 6318011,
        "line": 235835,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap35/p@215978",
        "anchor": "sceneV_35.10"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "AENEAS.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "troilus-and-cressida/sceneV_35.10/p@216060",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "TROILUS.\nYou understand me not that tell me so.\nI do not speak of flight, of fear of death,\nBut dare all imminence that gods and men\nAddress their dangers in. Hector is gone.\nWho shall tell Priam so, or Hecuba?\nLet him that will a screech-owl aye be call’d\nGo in to Troy, and say there ‘Hector’s dead.’\nThere is a word will Priam turn to stone;\nMake wells and Niobes of the maids and wives,\nCold statues of the youth; and, in a word,\nScare Troy out of itself. But, march away;\nHector is dead; there is no more to say.\nStay yet. You vile abominable tents,\nThus proudly pight upon our Phrygian plains,\nLet Titan rise as early as he dare,\nI’ll through and through you. And, thou great-siz’d coward,\nNo space of earth shall sunder our two hates;\nI’ll haunt thee like a wicked conscience still,\nThat mouldeth goblins swift as frenzy’s thoughts.\nStrike a free march to Troy. With comfort go;\nHope of revenge shall hide our inward woe.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
